# Copy this file to `.env` for local Expo runs. Never commit a real `.env`
# (it is gitignored). Do not paste keys into chat or GitHub.
#
# Windows: the file must be named exactly `.env` (not `.env.txt`).
# Notepad often appends .txt — Save As with name ".env" in quotes, or turn on
# "File name extensions" in Explorer and rename. Then restart:
#   npx expo start -c
# Installable build (preferred; not Expo Go):
#   npx expo start --dev-client

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (preferred phone path — cloud only, like LightLift)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# With these two set, signup / login / homes / ledger talk to Supabase directly.
# No laptop API and no EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL / LAN IP required for that happy path.
#
# Dev/test tip: Supabase → Authentication → Providers → Email → Confirm email → OFF
# so sign-up returns a session immediately (no inbox wait).
#
# Option A — Expo public names (typical local .env):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_ANON_KEY

# Option B — Cursor / Cloud secrets (EXPO_PUBLIC_ names are reserved in
# Cursor bind-app-secrets). app.config.js maps these onto Expo public names.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_ANON_KEY

# Never put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY in the phone app.
# Schema + founder steps: ../../supabase/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HomeAsset API (optional — local SQLite demo OR hosted AI / jobs)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed when Supabase URL + anon are set (cloud signup/login).
# Simulator / same PC without Supabase: leave unset (defaults to localhost:8787).
# Physical phone on the SQLite demo path only — use your PC LAN IPv4:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8787
#
# Windows — find the IP: Command Prompt → ipconfig → IPv4 under Wi‑Fi / Ethernet.
# AI assist still needs a reachable API URL when you want those features.
